        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          <div><div><font color="#000000">Human missions in space are
generally going to be of longer and longer duration. Given the upcoming long-term
manned missions first to the Moon and later to Mars, there will be an
increasing need to ensure that astronauts not only physically survive their
missions, but also thrive while missions go on. VR Mental Care is proposed as a
tailored and holistic gateway to maintain and improve the astronauts’ mental
health and thereby also leading to a positive impact on their physical
wellbeing and performance.<o:p></o:p></font></div></div><div><font color="#000000"><br></font></div><div><span style="font-family: "Open Sans", "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;"><font color="#000000">The VR Mental Care investigation demonstrates the application of virtual reality (VR) for mental relaxation, using 360° high quality (HQ) VR video and sound scenarios delivered via a VR headset. The overall aim is to use VR technology to provide a positive impact on the general mental health of astronauts during a space mission. Investigation activities consist of in-flight testing sessions comprised of VR video viewing and questionnaires (via the ESA EveryWear app).</font></span></div><div><span style="font-family: "Open Sans", "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;"><font color="#000000"><b><br></b></font></span></div><div><span style="font-family: "Open Sans", "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;"><font color="#000000"><b>Objective:</b></font></span></div><div><span style="font-family: "Open Sans", "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;"><font color="#000000"><br></font></span></div><div><div><font color="#000000">In summary the specific goals and
detailed objectives can be summarized as:<o:p></o:p></font></div><div><font color="#000000"><br></font></div>

<div><font color="#000000">1) Establish the efficacy of VR
for generating a positive effect on astronaut mental health, physical&nbsp;<span style="text-align: center; font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight);">wellbeing and performance.</span></font></div><div><span style="text-align: center; font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight);"><font color="#000000"><br></font></span></div><div><font color="#000000"><span style="text-align: center; font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight);">2) To utilize the application to perform
functional testing in orbit of the selected VR Headset to&nbsp;</span><span style="text-align: center; font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); font-size: 11pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: Calibri, sans-serif;">verify the performance of the selected&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: center;">VR headset</span></font></div><div><b><font color="#000000"><br></font></b></div><div><font color="#000000"><b>Technical objective</b>&nbsp;</font></div><div><font color="#000000"><br></font></div><div><font color="#000000">&nbsp;Develop, certify, and upload a VR headset capable of functioning in the&nbsp;<span style="text-align: center; font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight);">microgravity environment and for
delivering the VR Mental Care HQ film sessions.</span></font></div>

<div><b><font color="#000000"><br></font></b></div><div><font color="#000000"><b>Scientific Objective</b>&nbsp;</font></div><div><font color="#000000"><br></font></div><div><font color="#000000">Document the influence of the VR sessions by measured physical parameters&nbsp;<span style="text-align: center; font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight);">indicative of the astronaut´s mood
and wellbeing, together with the astronaut’s self-reported experience.</span></font></div></div>
        </div>

